The Archive by Imtiaz is a project built around the idea of intellectual comfort
A residential complex is appearing in the Dubai Land Residence Complex, where the library is not a decorative detail in the lobby, but part of the overall concept of the project.
The Archive by Imtiaz combines the familiar amenities of a modern residential complex with spaces for reading, concentration and creativity. There is a library, reading lounge and writer's room, and for more active recreation there is mini golf, a playground, a pet area, floating cabins and outdoor lounges on the podium levels.
Why you should pay attention to the project
Location. DLRC is located next to Sheikh Mohammed Bin Zayed Road and Al Ain Road. Downtown Dubai and Business Bay are about 20 minutes away, Dubai International Airport is about 25 minutes.
Format for life. The infrastructure is designed not only for a spectacular presentation of the project, but also for different scenarios of everyday life: work, reading, relaxation, sports and time with family.
Investment scenario. The development of DLRC and transport accessibility make the area interesting for buyers considering long-term rentals and the potential for growth in property values.
Terms of purchase. The project can be seen as an entry option into Dubailand's new developments with a fixed payment plan.
